{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The scepter shall not depart from Judah.</b> The scepter of greatness shall not depart from Judah until David comes, who is the beginning of the kingship of Judah. And so it was — do you not see that the banner of Judah journeys first? Also HaShem said, Judah shall go up first." "<b>And the meaning of מחוקק.</b> A scribe, for he inscribes in a book." "<b>And the meaning of מבין רגליו.</b> For thus is the way of every scribe, to sit between the feet of the officer." "<b>Shiloh.</b> Some say, in the manner of one translating into Aramaic, it means 'that which is his.' Some say it is from the root ובשליתה (Deuteronomy 28:57). Some derive it from the language of our early Sages of blessed memory: שליל. Some interpret it as referring to the city of Shiloh, and interpret יבוא like ובא השמש (Leviticus 22:7), or 'until the end of Shiloh comes,' for thus it is written, ויטוש משכן שילה (Psalms 78:60), and afterward, ויבחר בדוד עבדו (Psalms 78:70) — this too is not far-fetched. Or שילה may be like 'his son,' the heh in place of the vav, as in בתוך אהלה (Genesis 9:21), from the root לא תשלה אותי (2 Kings 4:28), whose meaning is 'you will not give birth.'" "<b>And the word יקהת.</b> Like ליקהת אם (Proverbs 30:17), and the yod serves for the future. Its meaning is that nations shall submit to his authority, and so were many peoples under the hand of David and Solomon his son. And the sense of עד כי יבא שילה is not that the scepter shall depart from him when Shiloh comes; rather its sense is like 'so-and-so will not lack bread until the time comes when he has fields and many vineyards.' And like it: כי לא אעזבך עד אשר אם עשיתי את אשר דברתי לך (Genesis 28:15) — He will return him to the land."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:29.189352047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}